00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:31.260
- [Mark] One?
- [Jennifer] Yeah.

00:09:31.260 --> 00:09:32.560
- [Mark] So you've gone
from six down to one?

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:33.891
- [Jennifer] Yeah.

00:09:33.891 --> 00:09:34.724
- [Mark] And you look much better.

00:09:34.724 --> 00:09:35.557
- [Jennifer] Yeah.

00:09:35.557 --> 00:09:36.410
- [Mark] Mentally--

00:09:36.410 --> 00:09:38.478
- [Jennifer] I've gained a little weight.

00:09:38.478 --> 00:09:43.290
- [Mark] Yeah, you seem a
little more healthier, calmer.

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:44.123
Your skin looks better.

00:09:44.123 --> 00:09:45.280
Everything looks better.

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:48.350
- [Jennifer] I'm hungry right
now though. Very hungry.

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:50.100
- [Mark] I'll set you
up with something here.

00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:52.680
Did you do this on your
own or through a program?

00:09:52.680 --> 00:09:53.977
Or how do you do it?

00:09:53.977 --> 00:09:54.810
- [Jennifer] On my own.

00:09:54.810 --> 00:09:55.643
- [Mark] You did this by yourself?

00:09:55.643 --> 00:09:56.476
- [Jennifer] Mm-hmm.

00:09:56.476 --> 00:09:57.309
- [Mark] What would you
recommend to somebody

00:09:57.309 --> 00:09:58.630
trying to get off of heroin?

00:09:58.630 --> 00:09:59.953
- [Jennifer] Go to a meeting.

00:10:02.853 --> 00:10:03.700
- [Mark] You know how
many people I've talked to

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:05.020
in the in the 10 years
I've been doing this

00:10:05.020 --> 00:10:07.590
that have kicked heroin?

00:10:07.590 --> 00:10:09.430
Honestly, they've told
me they've kicked heroin

00:10:09.430 --> 00:10:11.730
but the ones that have
actually done it, zero.

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:14.650
Maybe one.

00:10:14.650 --> 00:10:15.483
You'll be the first one

00:10:15.483 --> 00:10:16.730
that I'm seeing actually happen with.

00:10:16.730 --> 00:10:18.320
- [Jennifer] Yeah, I did on my own.

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:19.700
I got tired of living like that.

00:10:19.700 --> 00:10:20.910
- [Mark] So you weaned yourself slowly?

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:21.810
- [Jennifer] Yeah.

00:10:22.790 --> 00:10:24.590
And then with methadone, it helped.

00:10:24.590 --> 00:10:26.236
- [Mark] Oh, you're doing methadone too?

00:10:26.236 --> 00:10:27.700
- [Jennifer] Yeah.
Methadone saves my life.

00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:28.653
It saved my life.

00:10:30.111 --> 00:10:31.840
- [Mark] 'Cause you didn't tell that.

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:34.793
- Yeah, methadone. I've been
on methadone since 2014.

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:38.808
I didn't even go and get that today,

00:10:38.808 --> 00:10:39.780
it's because it's too late.

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:40.630
- [Mark] And then

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:45.246
what's the long-term plan with methadone?

00:10:45.246 --> 00:10:46.893
- Methadone is slowly decreased.

00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:49.240
- [Mark] And eventually
you'll be off that?

00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:50.240
- Yeah.

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:53.000
If I could get off that
methadone, I would be so happy.

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:54.200
'Cause it fucks you up.

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:55.490
It fucks you up.

00:10:55.490 --> 00:10:56.640
It fucks your bones up.

00:10:56.640 --> 00:10:58.500
It sets in your bones.

00:10:58.500 --> 00:11:00.198
- [Mark] And I'm sure there's a--

00:11:00.198 --> 00:11:02.550
- Give you arthritis really bad.

00:11:02.550 --> 00:11:04.743
You know who started that, right? Hitler.

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:06.413
For his people,

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:08.683
his army.

00:11:09.870 --> 00:11:10.703
- [Mark] Giving them methadone?

00:11:10.703 --> 00:11:11.620
- Yeah.

00:11:11.620 --> 00:11:13.660
To help him up with the pain.

00:11:13.660 --> 00:11:14.910
- [Mark] Really?
- Yeah.

00:11:16.840 --> 00:11:18.010
And now the federal
government gives it to us.

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:18.843
- [Mark] And you have kids, right?

00:11:18.843 --> 00:11:19.780
- Yeah.

00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:21.290
My daughter's a brain surgeon.

00:11:21.290 --> 00:11:22.270
- [Mark] Really?
- Yeah.

00:11:22.270 --> 00:11:23.770
- [Mark] Where?
- USC.

00:11:23.770 --> 00:11:25.306
- [Mark] Awesome.
- Yeah.

00:11:25.306 --> 00:11:26.195
- [Mark] And she knows you're down here?

00:11:26.195 --> 00:11:27.028
- Yeah.

00:11:27.028 --> 00:11:27.950
She's waiting for me to,

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:30.350
tell her to come and pick me up mom.

00:11:30.350 --> 00:11:31.183
- [Mark] You're almost there.

00:11:31.183 --> 00:11:32.870
- Yeah, I'm almost there.

00:11:32.870 --> 00:11:34.640
- [Mark] That's great.

00:11:34.640 --> 00:11:38.980
- She calls me, I got her on speed dial.

00:11:38.980 --> 00:11:39.890
- [Mark] So you talk to your daughter?

00:11:39.890 --> 00:11:41.470
- Yeah, every day.

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:42.303
- [Mark] Every day?

00:11:42.303 --> 00:11:43.960
- Every day.
- [Mark] That's great.

00:11:43.960 --> 00:11:46.117
- Even if I'm all fucked up I'll be like,

00:11:46.117 --> 00:11:47.440
"You don't want to talk to me right now."

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:49.797
And she's like, "Mom, I don't care.

00:11:49.797 --> 00:11:50.740
"I don't care."

00:11:50.740 --> 00:11:51.930
- [Mark] She doesn't care?
- No.

00:11:51.930 --> 00:11:52.763
- [Mark] That's great.

00:11:52.763 --> 00:11:53.870
- Yeah.

00:11:53.870 --> 00:11:54.703
- [Mark] That's beautiful.

00:11:54.703 --> 00:11:56.280
- She's helped me.

00:11:56.280 --> 00:11:58.070
- [Mark] No, I think that acceptance

00:11:58.070 --> 00:11:59.943
and non judgemental interaction.

00:12:01.181 --> 00:12:02.180
It works miracle--

00:12:02.180 --> 00:12:04.380
- She's like a best
friend that I never had.

00:12:06.300 --> 00:12:10.012
She says like, "But mom,
there's rats down here, really?"

00:12:10.012 --> 00:12:13.067
(Jennifer and Mark laugh)

00:12:13.067 --> 00:12:14.060
- [Mark] Yes, there are.

00:12:14.060 --> 00:12:15.410
- Yeah, she just turned 32.

00:12:17.810 --> 00:12:18.643
- [Mark] She's a brain surgeon?

00:12:18.643 --> 00:12:19.476
- Yeah.

00:12:19.476 --> 00:12:20.725
- [Mark] Wow.

00:12:20.725 --> 00:12:22.023
- She'll never be without a job.

00:12:23.050 --> 00:12:23.980
She got top honors.

00:12:23.980 --> 00:12:26.493
She was a Valedictorian of her class.

00:12:28.330 --> 00:12:30.896
She was like number two in the class.

00:12:30.896 --> 00:12:32.446
- [Mark] And she was raised by...

00:12:32.446 --> 00:12:33.279
- Me.

00:12:33.279 --> 00:12:34.112
- [Mark] You raised her?
- Yeah.

00:12:34.112 --> 00:12:36.658
- [Mark] So you've been living
on the streets since when?

00:12:36.658 --> 00:12:38.154
- Yeah, since

00:12:38.154 --> 00:12:38.987
1985.

00:12:42.710 --> 00:12:44.700
- [Mark] So '85, she was how old?

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:46.763
- She was... I had her in '88.

00:12:49.010 --> 00:12:50.260
- [Mark] So hold on.

00:12:50.260 --> 00:12:52.006
You were homeless when
you had your daughter?

00:12:52.006 --> 00:12:52.839
- Yeah.

00:12:52.839 --> 00:12:54.600
- [Mark] And you raised her where?

00:12:54.600 --> 00:12:57.390
- Well, through family,

00:12:57.390 --> 00:12:59.050
through my aunts and stuff.

00:12:59.050 --> 00:13:01.214
She would come with me
for a little while and--

00:13:01.214 --> 00:13:02.151
- [Mark] But she wasn't
staying on Skid Row?

00:13:02.151 --> 00:13:03.610
- No, no, no, no, no, no.

00:13:03.610 --> 00:13:04.500
- [Mark] She was staying with family?

00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:05.333
- Yeah.

00:13:05.333 --> 00:13:06.922
- [Mark] And then you would come and go?

00:13:06.922 --> 00:13:07.755
- Yeah.

00:13:07.755 --> 00:13:08.588
- [Mark] All right, so.

00:13:08.588 --> 00:13:09.421
So you had some help?

00:13:09.421 --> 00:13:10.510
- Yeah.

00:13:10.510 --> 00:13:11.343
- [Mark] That's great.

00:13:11.343 --> 00:13:12.499
But you certainly was
doing something, right?

00:13:12.499 --> 00:13:15.050
- My kids were never into foster
homes or nothing like that.

00:13:15.050 --> 00:13:17.093
They don't know nothing about that.

00:13:19.759 --> 00:13:23.610
They don't judge me for
being in the drug world.

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:26.200
She says, "Mom, everybody
has her skeletons."

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:27.140
- [Mark] Don't you as an addict,

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:30.150
feel like that's almost
the most important element

00:13:30.150 --> 00:13:31.460
in recovery?

00:13:31.460 --> 00:13:33.721
- Yeah. Not to judge.

00:13:33.721 --> 00:13:35.274
- [Mark] To not be made to feel bad.

00:13:35.274 --> 00:13:37.050
- [Jennifer] And you don't
forget where you come from too.

00:13:37.050 --> 00:13:37.883
- [Mark] I'm sorry.

00:13:37.883 --> 00:13:39.623
- [Jennifer] You don't
forget where you come from.

00:13:39.623 --> 00:13:40.456
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:13:40.456 --> 00:13:41.750
- [Jennifer] You can
always end up back there.

00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:44.743
Every time you fall, it's that much worse.

00:13:46.157 --> 00:13:47.490
I've made 25 steps...

00:13:47.490 --> 00:13:50.343
I'll take 100 steps and then come back 50.

00:13:51.725 --> 00:13:52.808
- [Mark] Yep.

00:13:53.760 --> 00:13:55.270
Well, Jennifer, it's so great to see you.

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:56.103
- Thank you.

00:13:56.103 --> 00:13:57.435
- [Mark] I see you all the time but--

00:13:57.435 --> 00:13:59.013
- Thank you for listening to me.

00:13:59.013 --> 00:14:00.380
(Mark and Jennifer laugh)

00:14:00.380 --> 00:14:01.213
- [Mark] You're amazing.

00:14:01.213 --> 00:14:03.200
I'm so proud of you.
- Thanks.

00:14:03.200 --> 00:14:04.300
- [Mark] And I'm proud
of your daughter too.

00:14:04.300 --> 00:14:05.393
- [Jennifer] Thank you.

00:14:05.393 --> 00:14:06.840
I'ma bring her down here.

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:08.150
I'm gonna bring her...

00:14:08.150 --> 00:14:09.970
Well, maybe go have lunch or something.

00:14:09.970 --> 00:14:11.332
- [Mark] That'd be cool.

00:14:11.332 --> 00:14:12.832
I'd love it here.

